<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#FFFFFF" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* No static <title> here: every page supplies its own through <PageTitle>, and with
       prerendering the HeadOutlet emits a real <title> element into this head. *@
    <meta name="description" content="bit BevTools (Bit.BevTools) - in-app developer tools for Blazor: a live component tree, a render profiler that explains why a component rendered, a timeline, state, network, JS interop, errors, DI and circuit diagnostics." />

    @* Link previews: the card a chat client or a social site unfurls is the first impression a
       shared link makes. *@
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Bit.BevTools" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="BevTools - in-app developer tools for Blazor" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="See why every component rendered, what each click cost, which request failed and which service is registered wrong - inside the running app, with no changes to its source." />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />

    <ResourcePreloader />
    @* The site kit (app.css, theme.js, site.js - shared by every Utilities demo), then this demo's
       own sample styles. BevTools' own stylesheet has no tag here: the panel links it itself, the
       way it does in any application. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["demo.css"]" />
    @* Scoped-CSS bundle: includes the client project's *.razor.css files as well. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["Bit.BevTools.Demo.Server.styles.css"]" />
    @* Synchronous on purpose: applies the light/dark theme before first paint. *@
    <script src="@Assets["theme.js"]"></script>
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveAuto" />
</head>

@* data-enhance-nav="false": a link followed before the runtime has started - the Blazor Server
   circuit on a first visit, the WebAssembly runtime once it is cached - is a plain page load rather
   than an enhanced one. Enhanced navigation fetches and merges the next page while the runtime is
   still starting, and the router the runtime then attaches can render the address it read before
   the merge - the URL says /getting-started and the page is the landing page. Once the app is
   interactive its router handles every link itself and this attribute is not consulted. *@
<body data-enhance-nav="false">
    @* InteractiveAuto, as the scenarios need: a first visit runs on a Blazor Server circuit (the
       Circuit page and the reconnect UI depend on it), and once the WebAssembly runtime is cached
       the same pages run in the browser, so both render paths can be inspected. *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveAuto" />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <div id="blazor-error-ui" data-nosnippet>
        An unhandled error has occurred.
        <a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
        <span class="dismiss">&#128473;</span>
    </div>
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["site.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
